# Construction LB+ (proofs/lb_last_step.md) run by src/lbplus.c through src/lb_owner.py --bin=lbplus. Every run: LB+ exactly as in the proof, every lemma asserted (assert_fail), every output checked against the raw EFX0 definition in construct.c (raw_fail). Columns: runs; c2 = no owner needed; owner_r = owner r (Theorem A); rotated = the bad case, repaired by one rotation (Theorem B), then rot_c2 (no owner needed) or rot_owner_k (owner k); r_E_nonempty = runs with an exposed agent w.r.t. r; rot_len_ge2 = rotations along a chain of >= 2 steps; max_large = largest bundle. Modes: 0 = LB's own Phase 1; 1 = every sequence of insertion choices (LB's R1 order); 2 = random insertion and R1 choices (--seed, --reps runs per profile). --random=COUNT:SEED = random non-core instances (every agent a uniformly random 3-set of the m goods) instead of the cores.
# PRELIMINARY: runs completed so far; the remaining sections are appended when they finish.

